# Security Principles

Follow these principles to build secure applications.

## Security by Design

- Consider security from the beginning of development.
- Validate and sanitize all inputs.
- Use parameterized queries to prevent SQL injection.
- Implement proper authentication and authorization.
- Follow the principle of least privilege.

## Input Validation

- Validate all user inputs at boundaries.
- Sanitize data before processing or storing.
- Use type checking and validation libraries.
- Reject invalid inputs early.
- Never trust client-side validation alone.

## Authentication & Authorization

- Implement secure authentication mechanisms.
- Use secure session management.
- Implement proper authorization checks.
- Use role-based access control (RBAC) when appropriate.
- Never expose sensitive credentials in code or logs.

## Defense in Depth

- Implement multiple layers of security.
- Don't rely on a single security measure.
- Validate at multiple levels (client, server, database).
- Log security events for monitoring.
- Implement rate limiting to prevent abuse.

## Data Protection

- Encrypt sensitive data at rest and in transit.
- Use HTTPS for all communications.
- Implement proper CORS policies.
- Protect against common vulnerabilities (XSS, CSRF, etc.).
- Keep dependencies up to date to patch security vulnerabilities.
